  {
    "id": "core:interior/the_saltmound",
    "name": "The Saltmound",
    "scene": "res://world/sites/site_interior.tscn",
    "kind": "deep_place",
    "place": "core:poi/the_saltmound",
    "danger": 3,
    "formed_by": "builder",
    "resident": "the Free Salters in their galleries, carrying the Charter's salt out four stone at a time; a Hushed sayer to keep the cut quiet from the gate; drakes come up from the brine; and the Salt-King on his throne of sacks in the heart of the mound",
    "story": "Six years of digging from the water side, into the heart of the Charter's salt: galleries hacked out of it and left standing white, a brine-pool where the Mere seeps in and the salt dissolves, the Salters' camp with its pay-board, a hall they cut up to the summit for air, and in the middle the counting-floor where every sack is weighed out to four stone before it goes to the boats. The Salt-King sits beyond it in a round hall walled with the Charter's own sacks, stacked like masonry, and the gulls' feet can be heard on the top of the mound overhead.",
    "unique_object": "the Salt-King's throne, built of the Charter's sealed sacks with the Row's wax still whole on every one, and his crown of salt crystals grown on a wire in the brine-pool",
