  {
    "id": "core:interior/the_drowned_quarter",
    "name": "The Drowned Quarter",
    "scene": "res://world/sites/site_interior.tscn",
    "kind": "deep_place",
    "place": "core:poi/fathom_shears",
    "danger": 3,
    "formed_by": "builder",
    "resident": "the Patience's lost crew, holding their breath and walking slowly; drakes in the dry vaults; the Company's chainman in the Singing Gallery with the bell-chain round his arms; and Corwen Lisle in the bell-hall, striking the Undersong",
    "story": "Forty fathom under the Mere west of Tollmere, the Builders' streets still stand, dry, the water stopped at their doors like a held breath. The Patience sets down on the Bell Street; from it the way goes down past a galleried nave where the Quarter's water stands at the door, the salvors' camp where they slept between dives, a hall of niches with the Quarter's dead in them, and the Singing Stair to the gallery and the bell-hall, where the Undersong hangs and Corwen Lisle strikes it every hour with its own tongue.",
    "unique_object": "the Undersong, the Quarter's great bell, hanging in its black frame at the bottom of the Singing Stair with its tongue out of it, still ringing",
    "site": {
      "kind": "ruined_hall",
